WEBVTT

00:52:28.963 --> 00:52:31.688
walking through the world with me
and making me different.

00:52:31.712 --> 00:52:32.881
We can have that.

00:52:32.905 --> 00:52:35.185
But I don't pretend to know
much more than that.

00:52:35.209 --> 00:52:38.584
I think it's insulting to people to ...

00:52:38.608 --> 00:52:40.042
file it under "mystery."

00:52:40.066 --> 00:52:42.302
CA: I mean, anyone who
has been through grief

00:52:42.326 --> 00:52:44.881
can understand why there is
a belief in the afterlife.

00:52:44.905 --> 00:52:46.074
EG: Sure.

00:52:46.098 --> 00:52:47.958
CA: You can certainly think of it as

00:52:47.982 --> 00:52:52.453
humans desperately wanting to believe
in that as a way of dulling the pain.

00:52:52.477 --> 00:52:56.761
But I think what you just said
is another, I would say,

00:52:56.785 --> 00:52:58.232
more profound response.

00:52:58.256 --> 00:53:00.716
I mean, certainly for me,
what made the difference